    {
      "id": "b_gpu_bridge",
      "name": "gpu_bridge",
      "tier": "T1",
      "moduleName": "gpu_bridge",
      "description": "Bridge from the SoC's memory stage to the GPU's host bus. Inputs: gpu_we (a store to the GPU window that is really happening), gpu_re (a load from it that is really happening), addr (32 bits, the access address), wdata (32, the store data), memtype (3, the access type: 2 is a word; 6 and 7 are reserved codes that act as a word; every other code is narrower or no access), host_rdata (32) and host_rvalid from the host bus. Outputs: host_en, host_we, host_addr (32), host_wdata (32) to the host bus, and rdata (32), what a load from the window returns. Translation, with off = addr bits 23:0: off from 000000 to 00FFFF hexadecimal is mapped to host address 30000000 | off bits 15:0 (control registers); 010000 to 0107FF to off bits 10:0, zero-extended (instruction memory); 020000 to 021FFF to 10000000 | off bits 12:0 (global memory); 030000 to 030FFF to 20000000 | off bits 11:0 (shared memory); 100000 to 1257FF to 40000000 | off bits 17:0 (video memory); 140000 to 1657FF to 40040000 | off bits 17:0 (depth memory); 180000 to 1807FF to 50000000 | off bits 10:0 (texture). Every other off is unmapped. host_addr is the mapped host address, 0 when unmapped. Outputs, at once: word = (memtype is 2, 6 or 7); host_we = mapped & gpu_we & word; host_en = host_we | (mapped & gpu_re); host_wdata = wdata; rdata = host_rdata when host_rvalid is 1, otherwise the register rdata_r. So a narrower store, or any access to an unmapped offset, is dropped. One register, rdata_r (32 bits): on each rising edge it becomes 0 when rst is 1, else takes host_rdata when host_rvalid is 1, else keeps its value. The host bus answers a read one cycle after the request (host_rvalid = 1 then), so a load returns the result of the previous GPU read and starts its own: a driver reads a GPU address twice and keeps the second value, and two loads in consecutive cycles work because the second sees host_rdata directly.",
